    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2Shdo2tBHRnXCft3zWGTffy)_\n\n## Merge order\n\n- Based on `main`; no dependencies.\n- Edits only `CHANGELOG.org` files and the `.org` docs; no code, no tangled block.\n- #442 (older CHANGELOG and DEVONthink doc update up to #440) overlaps this PR: close it or rebase it after this one.\n- Any open PR that adds a CHANGELOG line will conflict in `CHANGELOG.org`; the tidy owns those lines.\n\n## What\n\n- **Emacs `CHANGELOG.org`** (last tidy was #389 on 2026-11-11)\n  - Merged PRs #394 to #481 (except those only in the global file) in their feature sets, in dependency order, no repeated headings.\n  - New sets: citar candidates, reading PDFs (`sp-pdf-reader`), `sp-fetch-inbox`, echo-area hints, the vulpea-ui view frame, buffers/tabs/frames.\n  - \"Being developed\": the open PRs with their merge order (DEVONthink stack #418 → #419 → #420 → #421 → #451; #443 → #455; the rest on `main`).\n  - Direct commits on `main` since the tidy: `which-key` `:ensure nil` and the `test`/`course` tags; the hand edit 87a4fbb is under #423.\n- **Global `CHANGELOG.org`**\n  - DEVONthink open applet (#394, #444, #449), `gh-pr-pdf` (#401), fisher (#481), AeroSpace note (#447), the `dotfiles-prs` backup commits.\n- **Module docs** (23 docs): a \"Changes by pull request\" section added (sp-see-also, sp-tabs, sp-buffers, devonthink, reading, pdf-reader, fetch-inbox, bibsync, interaction, elpaca-melpa-fix) or extended (sp-academic, sp-org-lint, sp-vulpea, batch-report and others), as nested bullets.\n\n## Not verified\n\n- Written from the PR titles and bodies and the merge diffs; no Emacs here, so the `tangle` check was not run (only prose after the last code block changed).\n- Needs-testing flags come from the `needs-further-testing` label; #438, #442, #443, #446, #455 and the PRs opened after the 2026-11-14 backup have no label data.\n- Not read in full: PR bodies cut at about 1,100 characters, so some doc bullets (#409, #410, #414, #415, #424, #432) cover the main points only.\n- #458 (superseded) and #417 (replaced by #418) are left out.\n\nDocs only; no manual testing needed.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiCdFzdq4QWUuMSesFX\n",
